  "term": "respiratory sinus arrhythmia",
  "definition": "Respiratory sinus arrhythmia is a measure of heart-rate variation linked to breathing and to cardiac vagal activity. Its size is affected by breathing pattern, including how fast and how deeply a person breathes, so these influences may need to be taken into account in psychophysiology research.",
